      "hints": [
        "Set $\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{9}{2}x - 12 = 0$.",
        "Find $x = \\frac{8}{3}$ and evaluate $y = 2$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Differentiate $y = \\frac{9}{4}x^2 - 12x + 18$ with respect to $x$:\n$$\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{9}{2}x - 12$$",
        "Set $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 0$ and solve for $x$:\n$$\\frac{9}{2}x = 12 \\implies x = 12 \\times \\frac{2}{9} = \\frac{8}{3}$$",
        "Evaluate the minimum $y$-value at $x = \\frac{8}{3}$:\n$$y = \\frac{9}{4}\\left(\\frac{8}{3}\\right)^2 - 12\\left(\\frac{8}{3}\\right) + 18 = 16 - 32 + 18 = 2 \\implies \\left(\\frac{8}{3}, 2\\right)$$"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_id": "9709_w22_12_q11_b",
      "difficulty": 5,
      "mapping": {
        "topic_id": "9709_p1_t_integration",
        "lesson_id": "9709_p1_t_integration_m03_l01"
      },
      "hints": [
        "Integrate $\\int_0^4 (12x - \\frac{9}{4}x^2 - \\frac{3}{8}x^{5/2})\\,dx$.",
        "Evaluate $\\left[ 6x^2 - \\frac{3}{4}x^3 - \\frac{3}{28}x^{7/2} \\right]_0^4$.",
        "Calculate $48 - \\frac{96}{7} = \\frac{240}{7}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Set up the definite integral for the area between the two curves from $x = 0$ to $x = 4$:\n$$\\text{Area} = \\int_0^4 \\left( \\left(18 - \\frac{3}{8}x^{5/2}\\right) - \\left(\\frac{9}{4}x^2 - 12x + 18\\right) \\right)\\,dx$$",
        "Simplify the integrand:\n$$= \\int_0^4 \\left( 12x - \\frac{9}{4}x^2 - \\frac{3}{8}x^{5/2} \\right)\\,dx$$",
        "Integrate term-by-term:\n$$= \\left[ 6x^2 - \\frac{3}{4}x^3 - \\frac{3}{28}x^{7/2} \\right]_0^4$$",
        "Evaluate at upper limit $x = 4$:\n$$= 6(16) - \\frac{3}{4}(64) - \\frac{3}{28}(128) = 96 - 48 - \\frac{96}{7} = 48 - \\frac{96}{7} = \\frac{240}{7} \\approx 34.3$$"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_id": "9709_w22_12_q11_c",
      "difficulty": 2,
      "mapping": {
        "topic_id": "9709_p1_t_differentiation",
